    "q-223721": {
      "dom_id": "step-q223721",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "In **ascending order**, the solutions to $4{m}^{2}+5m=0$ are $m=${{field-1}} and $m=$\n{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{m}^{2}+5m & =0 \\\\ m(4m+5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the zero product rule to get\n\n$$\nm=0\\,\\text{or}\\,4m+5=0,\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives\n\n$$\nm=0\\,\\text{or}\\,m=-\\frac{5}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $m=-\\frac{5}{4}$ and $m=0.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
