    "q-223741": {
      "dom_id": "step-q223741",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "In **ascending order**, the solutions to $\\frac{2}{5}{z}^{2}=-2z$ are $z=${{field-1}} and $z=$\n{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we move all of the terms to the left-hand side and then factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}{z}^{2} & =-2z \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}{z}^{2}+2z & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}z(z+5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the zero product rule to get\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}z=0\\,\\text{or}\\,z+5=0,\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives\n\n$$\nz=0\\,\\text{or}\\,z=-5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $z=-5$ and $z=0.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
