    "q-220342": {
      "dom_id": "step-q220342",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "In **ascending order**, the solutions to $3{t}^{2}=\\frac{t}{3}$ are $t=${{field-1}} and $t=$\n{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we move all of the terms to the left-hand side and then factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2} & =\\frac{t}{3} \\\\ 3{t}^{2}-\\frac{t}{3} & =0 \\\\ t(3t-\\frac{1}{3}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the zero product rule to get\n\n$$\nt=0\\,\\text{or}\\,3t-\\frac{1}{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives\n\n$$\nt=0\\,\\text{or}\\,t=\\frac{1}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $t=0$ and $t=\\frac{1}{9}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
